1961
The mutable external-fact inventory becomes the general rule "External facts: unknown is not no": evidence of the exact route, unknown never withholds input, a refusal is an observation about one request, own transport limits named as ours, and the three executable guards; the vision prefix row is removed and the retired-default row describes only our own former-default migrations. The OpenRouter Anthropic parameter pin gets its own dated row as a declared exception of the name-invariance test.
